## Automation Architecture

An automation consists of five core components:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph triggers [Triggers]
        T1[Cron Schedule]
        T2[Git Event]
        T3[Slack Event]
        T4[Linear Event]
        T5[PagerDuty Event]
        T6[Sentry Event]
        T7[Webhook]
    end

    subgraph tools [Tools / Actions]
        A1[PR Comment]
        A2[Post to Slack]
        A3[Read Slack]
        A4[Request Reviewers]
        A5[Manage Check Run]
        A6[Use MCP Server]
    end

    subgraph prompts [Prompt / Instructions]
        P1[Agent Behavior]
        P2[Response Format]
        P3[Constraints]
    end

    subgraph config [Cloud Agent Config]
        C1[Model Selection]
        C2[Agent Options]
        C3[Memory]
    end

    T1 & T2 & T3 & T4 & T5 & T6 & T7 --> B[Trigger Fired]
    B --> A1 & A2 & A3 & A4 & A5 & A6
    P1 & P2 & P3 --> A1 & A2 & A3 & A4 & A5 & A6
    C1 & C2 & C3 --> B
```

### 1. Trigger

The event that starts the automation. An automation has exactly one trigger.

### 2. Tools (Actions)

Capabilities the agent has when the automation runs. Multiple tools can be enabled.

### 3. Prompt (Instructions)

Natural language instructions telling the agent what to do when the trigger fires.

### 4. Model

The AI model the agent uses to execute the automation.

### 5. Agent Options

Configuration for the Cloud Agent including memory, installation behavior, and other runtime settings.

