## Tool Types (Actions)

Tools define what the Cloud Agent can do when an automation runs.

| Tool Label | Proto Name | Description |
|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| Comment on PRs | `prComment` | Posts a comment on a GitHub/GitLab pull request |
| Post to Slack | `slack` | Sends a message to a Slack channel or DM |
| Read Slack | `readSlack` | Reads messages from a Slack channel |
| Request reviewers | `requestReviewers` | Requests code review from specified users |
| Manage check runs | `manageCheckRun` | Creates or updates a CI check run |
| Use MCP server | `mcp` | Calls an MCP server tool |

### Tool Configuration Examples

```yaml
# PR Comment action
workflow:
  actions:
    - prComment:
        action: COMMENTED
        body: "Automated review: code looks good."

# Slack action
workflow:
  actions:
    - slack:
        channel: "C0ABC123"
        message: "Deployment completed successfully."

# MCP action
workflow:
  actions:
    - mcp:
        server:
          name: "Linear"
        tool: "searchIssues"
        arguments:
          query: "critical bugs"
```

